Description: Amethyst and Amethyst-dark GTK3 themes (accent-parameterized, Adwaita-based)
 The Amethyst GTK3 themes, derived from the Adwaita and Adwaita-dark CSS
 files shipped in the GTK+ 3.24.43 source, parameterized for accent colors
 (named @accent_bg_color/@accent_color with shade()/mix() derivations).
 GTK3 ignores filesystem themes named "Adwaita" or "Adwaita-dark" (its
 built-in GResource versions are used instead), so the themes are named
 Amethyst and Amethyst-dark; selecting them makes the accent-color
 parameterization effective. A single user CSS override such as
 @define-color accent_bg_color <hex> (as written by GNOME Settings >
 Appearance) re-themes every accent use (selection, switches, checkboxes,
 suggested buttons, links, focus rings) at once. Defaults are the stock
 GNOME blue accents (light) and dark-blue accents (dark).

